(4625662, 663996, 52549, '<td valign="top">WTG, Oliver. Fabulous image.</td>', 'WTG, Oliver. Fabulous image.', '2008-04-09 03:16:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4625676, 663069, 30982, '<td valign="top">I really like the composition of this - the sweeping curve with that one blossom backed by those not yet opened.  As a quilter, I''d say this is a cool pink - but with fabrics we work in tones, not absolute color.  Based on the color wheel, reds and pinks are indeed warm colors, as is yellow.  I suspect even though people might not know why, they thought this "cool" rather than warm (I''ll look at comments in a minute).  To make it warmer - warmer light (though I like the quiet light you have) or a warmer background.  I suspect, though, had you stuck it in the cool challenge, you would have been told it was a "warm" color.</td>', 'I really like the composition of this - the sweeping curve with that one blossom backed by those not yet opened.  As a quilter, I''d say this is a cool pink - but with fabrics we work in tones, not absolute color.  Based on the color wheel, reds and pinks are indeed warm colors, as is yellow.  I suspect even though people might not know why, they thought this "cool" rather than warm (I''ll look at comments in a minute).  To make it warmer - warmer light (though I like the quiet light you have) or a warmer background.  I suspect, though, had you stuck it in the cool challenge, you would have been told it was a "warm" color.', '2008-04-09 03:25:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4625683, 664753, 30982, '<td valign="top">Soft, smooth, very painterly.  And you beat me big time in commenter''s average.  :-)</td>', 'Soft, smooth, very painterly.  And you beat me big time in commenter''s average.  :-)', '2008-04-09 03:28:12.000000', NULL, 0),
