(4629791, 663051, 61961, '<td valign="top">I think the hot pink is definitely warm enough.  Interesting against the cooler background (which has enough green to also warm it up a little).  Good DOF, and I like the composition, too.  Congrats, you did well, especially considering it''s a flower shot (there''s a lot of them in case you haven''t noticed).</td>', 'I think the hot pink is definitely warm enough.  Interesting against the cooler background (which has enough green to also warm it up a little).  Good DOF, and I like the composition, too.  Congrats, you did well, especially considering it''s a flower shot (there''s a lot of them in case you haven''t noticed).', '2008-04-10 10:43:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4629984, 664733, 33769, '<td valign="top">I asked to have myself DQ''ed after I realized that I used the clone stamp and it was a ''basic'' editing challenge (i was teeter-tottering between which challenge to enter it into the DNMC or something else -and got a bit confused; oh well- learn from ones mistakes! one of my mottos) <br/> <br/>these are wax-crayons (so the tip is very difficult to get to ''look'' in focus- i''ll definatly try to reshoot these sometime tho for the sillyness of it sometime) thank you all for your comments/suggestions! i appreciate the time you took to help me improve my art! <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-04-12 11:14:49.</i></td>', 'I asked to have myself DQ''ed after I realized that I used the clone stamp and it was a ''basic'' editing challenge (i was teeter-tottering between which challenge to enter it into the DNMC or something else -and got a bit confused; oh well- learn from ones mistakes! one of my mottos)  these are wax-crayons (so the tip is very difficult to get to ''look'' in focus- i''ll definatly try to reshoot these sometime tho for the sillyness of it sometime) thank you all for your comments/suggestions! i appreciate the time you took to help me improve my art! ', '2008-04-10 11:56:58.000000', '2008-04-12 12:14:49.000000', 0),
