(4636697, 664733, 57229, '<td valign="top">Hand held at 5.0<br/> <br/>If you mounted the camera (put it on a book or something, if you don''t have a tripod handy) you could close down the aperture, use a longer exposure and <u>gain the depth of field</u> that would allow you to have the tips in focus as well as the rest. Check it out.<br/> <br/>Nice idea, shame about the dq :-)</td>', 'Hand held at 5.0 If you mounted the camera (put it on a book or something, if you don''t have a tripod handy) you could close down the aperture, use a longer exposure and gain the depth of field that would allow you to have the tips in focus as well as the rest. Check it out. Nice idea, shame about the dq :-)', '2008-04-13 16:49:37.000000', NULL, 0),
