(4637265, 664733, 33769, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by raish:</b></div><hr/><i> Hand held at 5.0<br/> <br/>If you mounted the camera (put it on a book or something, if you don''t have a tripod handy) you could close down the aperture, use a longer exposure and <u>gain the depth of field</u> that would allow you to have the tips in focus as well as the rest. Check it out.<br/> <br/>Nice idea, shame about the dq :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Oh- I don''t mind the "DQ" I actually asked them to remove my image before the voting completed-because I realized it was a ''basic-editing'' and i used the clone-stamp (got confused, last minute clicked on an entry and didn''t pay full attention to what i was doing- i was originally gonna toss this into the DNMC challenge then changed my mind...which is where the ''duh'' occurred) :) <br/> <br/>the tips of these are very very ''soft'' they''re ''wax''  -- i''ll definatly try your suggestion sometime... they''re not actual ''pencils'' they''re wax crayons; silly random stuff i have laying around the house...<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by raish: Hand held at 5.0 If you mounted the camera (put it on a book or something, if you don''t have a tripod handy) you could close down the aperture, use a longer exposure and gain the depth of field that would allow you to have the tips in focus as well as the rest. Check it out. Nice idea, shame about the dq :-)   Oh- I don''t mind the "DQ" I actually asked them to remove my image before the voting completed-because I realized it was a ''basic-editing'' and i used the clone-stamp (got confused, last minute clicked on an entry and didn''t pay full attention to what i was doing- i was originally gonna toss this into the DNMC challenge then changed my mind...which is where the ''duh'' occurred) :)  the tips of these are very very ''soft'' they''re ''wax''  -- i''ll definatly try your suggestion sometime... they''re not actual ''pencils'' they''re wax crayons; silly random stuff i have laying around the house... ', '2008-04-13 22:28:45.000000', NULL, 0),
